/Title (The environmental impact of data centres will disproportionately affect lower socio-economic communities and regional/rural areas, compounding existing social and economic inequality: Many proposed data centres are seeking approval to be developed in regional and remote areas, particularly the Northern Territory. These are areas which are already disproportionately vulnerable to climate disasters \(e.g., heatwaves, bushfires, flooding, cyclones etc.\) and which face ongoing challenges in accessing adequate resources and infrastructure.)
